# Build output
/target
**/*.rs.bk
*.pdb

# Scratch files and directories. Research, toolchain experiments and commit-message
# files create these at the repository root; they are working state, never source.
#
# NO trailing slash: with one, this matched directories only, and a stray
# `.tmp-commit-msg` was committed on the first attempt. The pattern has to cover
# files too.
/.tmp-*

# Toolchain comparison output: raw benchmark text, regenerated on every run.
/xtask/toolchain-compare/out/

# Reference checkout of the upstream C++ implementation.
#
# It sits in the working tree purely so behaviour can be compared and so the
# provenance notes have something concrete to point at. It must NEVER enter
# version control:
#
#   * it is someone else's code, under someone else's licence, carrying an
#     unresolved DMCA claim -- committing it would import both problems into
#     this repository's history, where they cannot be removed by a later commit;
#   * `cargo package`/`cargo publish` would pick it up as stray files;
#   * a fork or a source tarball would redistribute it.
#
# Nothing under `crates/` or `xtask/` may read from this directory at build time.
/OpenHashTab/

# Local agent / AI-tooling guidance. Kept out of version control on purpose:
# it encodes the working rules for whoever is editing this checkout, including
# the provenance constraints, and is not part of the shipped product.
# NOTE: README.md links to CLAUDE.md, so an untracked checkout would have a
# dangling reference -- see the note in that file if you decide to publish it.
/CLAUDE.md

# Generated localization resources
/crates/rusthashtab-ui/src/generated/

# Installer build output
/installer/build/
*.msi
*.wixpdb

# Local, non-published research material and reference binaries.
#
# Scope is deliberate: only `docs/internal/` is ignored, NOT all of `docs/`.
# Ignoring `/docs/` would work today (nothing else lives there) and then silently
# swallow the first real document someone adds under `docs/`. The pattern has to
# name the part that is local-only.
/docs/internal/
/reference/
*.dll
!crates/**/tests/fixtures/**/*.dll

# `docs/internal/` is kept out of version control entirely. It is the research and
# decision record, it names the upstream project, and none of that belongs in the
# product's history. It lives on the developer's disk only.
#
# CONSEQUENCE, and it matters: a fresh clone has no docs/internal/. Nothing may
# require it to exist -- scripts and CI must treat it as optional, and anything
# that reads it has to degrade gracefully when it is absent. `cargo xtask check`
# validates it only when present.

# Editor / OS
.vs/
.vscode/
.idea/
*.user
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
